  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Good akara depends on a well-made "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "bean batter",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "bean-batter"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " beaten until it traps air. These fritters are the ancestor of Brazilian "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "acaraje ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "acaraje"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", carried west across the Atlantic with the slave trade. Serve straight from the oil."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Beat the batter vigorously by hand or in a stand mixer for 2 minutes after blending. This aeration makes the fritters light rather than dense."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "black-eyed-beans",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "dried, soaked overnight, skins rubbed off",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "onion",
              "amount": 0.5,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "roughly chopped",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "pepper-red",
              "amount": 0.5,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "roughly chopped",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "chilli-green",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "optional, for heat",
              "isOptional": true,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sea-salt-fine",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sunflower-oil",
              "amount": 500,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": "for deep frying",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blend peeled beans with onion, pepper, chilli and 2 tablespoons water until very smooth."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Transfer to a bowl. Add salt. Beat vigorously with a wooden spoon for 2 minutes until the batter lightens slightly in colour."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oil in a deep pan to 180C. Drop a small spoonful of batter in; it should sizzle and float immediately."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drop tablespoons of batter into the oil in batches of 4 to 5. Fry for 3 to 4 minutes, turning once, until deep golden brown."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drain on paper towels. Serve immediately."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Fritters fall apart in oil",
              "cause": "Batter too loose or oil not hot enough",
              "fix": "The batter should hold a soft mound when dropped from a spoon. If it spreads flat, add a tablespoon of chickpea flour. Ensure oil is at 180C before frying."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Fritters are dense and heavy",
              "cause": "Batter not beaten enough",
              "fix": "Beat for a full 2 minutes after blending. The batter should feel slightly spongy."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Akara is the quintessential Lagos breakfast, sold from roadside stalls alongside ogi (corn porridge) from early morning. The same dish appears in Ghana as koose and across the Sahel under various names. Its descendant acaraje is a street food institution in Bahia, Brazil, now registered as a cultural heritage item by UNESCO."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}